    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ramapo/jobs/5457006/graduate-assistant-office-of-grants-sponsored-programs": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Ramapo College of New Jersey Careers For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Graduate Assistant - Office of Grants & Sponsored Programs | Ramapo College of New Jersey Careers page has loaded. Graduate Assistant - Office of Grants & Sponsored Programs | Ramapo College of New Jersey Careers page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Ramapo College of New Jersey Careers powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Graduate Assistant - Office of Grants & Sponsored Programs Print Apply ﻿ Graduate Assistant - Office of Grants & Sponsored Programs Salary See Position Description Location Ramapo College, Main Campus - Mahwah NJ Job Type Graduate Assistant Job Number 202300445 Core Teaching & Learning Core Department Grants Office Opening Date 08/21/2026 FLSA Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit NA Description Benefits Questions Description About Ramapo College of New Jersey Ramapo College of New Jersey is the state’s premier public liberal arts college, where students build the confidence, skills, and perspective to thrive in a changing world. Located on a breathtaking 300-acre campus in the foothills of the Ramapo Mountains and just a short trip from New York City, Ramapo blends the best of both worlds: natural beauty, state-of-the-art facilities, and access to one of the world’s most dynamic job markets. With approximately 6,000 students, Ramapo offers a personalized, student-centered experience defined by a 16:1 student–faculty ratio, small classes, and faculty who mentor, challenge, and inspire. Students can explore over 40 undergraduate majors and a growing portfolio of graduate programs in fields such as Business Administration, Data Science, Nursing, Educational Leadership, Social Work, Special Education, and the Doctor of Nursing Practice. Across every discipline, Ramapo emphasizes hands-on learning through internships, co-ops, study abroad, faculty research, service projects, and real-world experiences that prepare students for meaningful careers. Our campus is home to cutting-edge academic spaces, including the Anisfield School of Business, the Adler Center for Nursing Excellence, the Sharp Sustainability Education Center, the Berrie Center for Performing and Visual Arts, the Les Paul Music Studio, and the Peter P. Mercer Learning Commons. Ramapo’s award-winning residence halls are consistently ranked among the best in New Jersey. Nationally recognized for excellence and value, Ramapo is ranked #1 among New Jersey public colleges by College Choice, named a Best Regional University North by U.S. News & World Report , and celebrated by Kiplinger’s , Money Magazine , Colleges of Distinction, and Victory Media’s Military Friendly rankings. At Ramapo, students don’t just earn degrees; they discover their strengths, explore new possibilities, and build the foundation for bold futures. Working at Ramapo Ramapo College of New Jersey has been recognized as a “Great College to Work For,” where our employees are at the heart of everything we do. We foster an equitable and fair workplace where ideas are welcomed, contributions are valued, and individuals are encouraged to grow both professionally and personally. Employees benefit from meaningful work, opportunities for development, and the chance to make a lasting impact on students’ lives every day. At Ramapo College, we believe excellence is achieved through teamwork, respect, accountability, innovation, and a shared commitment to learning. Our all-hands-on-deck culture requires leadership at all levels to ensure we achieve our mission, implement our goals, and invest in our future one student at a time. We are proud to offer a supportive environment that values well-being and continuous improvement.  We believe in being bold, being kind, and being good teammates, making Ramapo not just a place to work, but a great place to belong. Ramapo College offers outstanding benefits through the New Jersey State Benefits system, generous PTO, professional development opportunities, wellness programs, tuition discounts for employees and their dependents, and much more. Examples of Duties Compensation: This is a 10-month, part-time Graduate Assistant position that requires 20 hours per week. Compensation includes a $10,000 stipend and up to $8,000 in tuition reimbursement. Period of Contract: September 2026 -June 2027 (renewable); 20 hours per week JOB SUMMARY The Graduate Assistant supports the Office of Grants & Sponsored Programs (OGSP) by assisting with grant administration activities and Institutional Review Board (IRB) operations. This position provides hands-on experience in research administration, sponsored programs, compliance, and research ethics while supporting faculty, staff, and students throughout the proposal development and human subjects research processes. Working closely with the Director of the Office of Grants & Sponsored Programs and the Chair of the Institutional Review Board (faculty), the graduate assistant will provide grants support by coordinating proposal development and internal submission processes. They will serve as the primary point of contact for student IRB submissions, facilitate communication between student investigators and the IRB Chair, develop educational communications, and assist with updating IRB forms, policies, consent templates, and procedures to promote compliance and continuous process improvement. The position also provides administrative support through data collection and reporting, maintenance of confidential records, and project management assistance. Duties/Responsibilities: Grants Administration Assist in coordinating proposal development timelines and internal submission deadlines. Assist with collecting institutional data, supporting documentation, and letters of support for grant proposals. Assist in preparing grant development resources, templates, checklists, and guidance documents. Help to ensure compliance with institutional and sponsor requirements. Institutional Review Board (IRB) Administration Develop and disseminate “Ethics Blasts” highlighting training opportunities (e.g., webinars, CITI modules, and other professional development resources) Support the planning and promotion of IRB-related workshops and trainings for students, faculty, and staff Serve as a liaison to the student body to increase awareness of research ethics and IRB processes Serve as the first point of contact for student IRB applications Liaise between IRB Chair and student applicants Assist in building and maintaining a library of consent form language and templates Support efforts to standardize and improve IRB forms and guidance documents Assist in coordinating recognition initiatives (e.g., invitations to campus events such as Scholars Day or Honors Symposium, appreciation materials, and engagement activities) Administrative & Office Support Assist with data collection, record keeping, and reporting for grants and IRB activities. Organize electronic files and maintain confidential records. Assist with office communications, event coordination, and project management activities. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Education/Experience: Requirements: Qualifications Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Experience with or willingness to learn data management tools (e.g., Google Sheets, Excel; Power BI a plus) Strong written communication skills, particularly for educational and web-based content Enrollment in a graduate program at Ramapo College or another college/university for a minimum of six (6) credit hours per semester or two (2) courses per semester, whichever is greater, during the academic year; Proof of course enrollment and good academic standing each semester; Active and satisfactory academic progress towards completion of a graduate degree in an approved graduate (Master’s) program with a transcript provided to the Supervisor(s)/Human Resources Department at the end of each semester; A minimum grade point average of 3.0 or higher; and Good academic standing during the term of the contract. Must be able to meet flexible work schedule requirements, in particular, nights and weekends. EDUCATION: Graduation from an accredited college with a Bachelor’s Degree. Supplemental Information EEO Statement Ramapo College is an Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Ramapo is committed to academic excellence through interdisciplinary and experiential learning and international and intercultural understanding.  Ramapo is also committed to fostering a community that inspires a culture of inclusivity. Examples can be found in its mission statement, strategic plans, degree and course offerings and other programs. Ramapo’s environment is welcoming, dedicated to social justice, and respectful of freedom of expression. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Are you enrolled in a Graduate Degree program beginning Fall 2026 semester? yes no Required Question Employer Ramapo College of New Jersey Address 505 Ramapo Valley Road Mahwah, New Jersey, 07430 Phone 2016847782 Website https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ramapo? Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opp