      "title": "Director of Nursing Programs",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Ramapo College of New Jersey Careers For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Director of Nursing Programs | Ramapo College of New Jersey Careers page has loaded. Director of Nursing Programs | Ramapo College of New Jersey Careers page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Ramapo College of New Jersey Careers powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Director of Nursing Programs Print Apply ﻿ Director of Nursing Programs Salary $100,000.00 - $145,000.00 Annually Location Ramapo College, Main Campus - Mahwah NJ Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202300383 Core Teaching & Learning Core Department Nursing Program Opening Date 04/16/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit MN Description Benefits Questions Description About Ramapo College of New Jersey Ramapo College of New Jersey is the state’s premier public liberal arts college, where students build the confidence, skills, and perspective to thrive in a changing world. Located on a breathtaking 300-acre campus in the foothills of the Ramapo Mountains and just a short trip from New York City, Ramapo blends the best of both worlds: natural beauty, state-of-the-art facilities, and access to one of the world’s most dynamic job markets. With approximately 6,000 students, Ramapo offers a personalized, student-centered experience defined by a 16:1 student–faculty ratio, small classes, and faculty who mentor, challenge, and inspire. Students can explore over 40 undergraduate majors and a growing portfolio of graduate programs in fields such as Business Administration, Data Science, Nursing, Educational Leadership, Social Work, Special Education, and the Doctor of Nursing Practice. Across every discipline, Ramapo emphasizes hands-on learning through internships, co-ops, study abroad, faculty research, service projects, and real-world experiences that prepare students for meaningful careers. Our campus is home to cutting-edge academic spaces, including the Anisfield School of Business, the Adler Center for Nursing Excellence, the Sharp Sustainability Education Center, the Berrie Center for Performing and Visual Arts, the Les Paul Music Studio, and the Peter P. Mercer Learning Commons. Ramapo’s award-winning residence halls are consistently ranked among the best in New Jersey. Nationally recognized for excellence and value, Ramapo is ranked #1 among New Jersey public colleges by College Choice, named a Best Regional University North by U.S. News & World Report , and celebrated by Kiplinger’s , Money Magazine , Colleges of Distinction, and Victory Media’s Military Friendly rankings. At Ramapo, students don’t just earn degrees; they discover their strengths, explore new possibilities, and build the foundation for bold futures. Working at Ramapo Ramapo College of New Jersey has been recognized as a “Great College to Work For,” where our employees are at the heart of everything we do. We foster an equitable and fair workplace where ideas are welcomed, contributions are valued, and individuals are encouraged to grow both professionally and personally. Employees benefit from meaningful work, opportunities for development, and the chance to make a lasting impact on students’ lives every day. At Ramapo College, we believe excellence is achieved through teamwork, respect, accountability, innovation, and a shared commitment to learning. Our all-hands-on deck culture requires leadership at all levels to ensure we achieve our mission, implement our goals, and invest in our future one student at a time. We are proud to offer a supportive environment that values well-being and continuous improvement.  We believe in being bold, being kind, and being good teammates, making Ramapo not just a place to work, but a great place to belong. Ramapo College offers outstanding benefits through the New Jersey State Benefits system, generous PTO, professional development opportunities, wellness programs, tuition discounts for employees and their dependents, and much more. Salary Range: Manager - D28 $100,000-$145,000 Job Summary: Director of Nursing Programs  (reporting to the Assistant Dean/Nursing) Ramapo College of New Jersey, a public liberal arts institution, seeks a dynamic and forward-thinking professional staff member (12 months) with a primary focus in Nursing reflecting a deep commitment to the College’s core academic pillars: international, intercultural, interdisciplinary, and experiential learning. We welcome scholars/administrators who are passionate about leading faculty and staff towards emerging technologies and AI into high-impact pedagogy and scholarship, and who bring both personal and professional dedication to student success. The ideal candidate is energized by community engagement and committed to the education of students from a broad range of backgrounds Ramapo proudly serves—including first-generation college students, as well as bi- and multilingual and multicultural learners of all ages. If you believe nursing programs should be inclusive, empowering, and transformative, we invite you to help shape the next chapter of Ramapo’s mission. Join us in building a future where every student thrives and your impact resonates far beyond the classroom. Let’s redefine what’s possible—together! Examples of Duties Duties Responsible for the overall management of the pre-licensure, RN/BSN, MSN and DNP programs, including curriculum oversight, evaluation and continual improvement as well as  faculty recruitment and scheduling. Ensures the provision of academic excellence and fostering of a supportive and inclusive environment for faculty and students Ensures that the program meets accreditation standards and regulatory requirements and remains current with professional standards and requirements. Oversees preparation for accreditation self studies, State Board reports, and site visits. Collaborates and acts as a liaison with clinical partners to maintain those relationships ensuring effective learning environments Leads faculty teams collaboratively ensuring innovative and supportive faculty environments. Supports student success through provision and evaluation of advisement, counseling and other student success services. Ensures appropriate and current affiliation and compliance data Collaborates across campus to efficiently and effectively meet the needs of the program and ensure the college mission and vision are aligned Implements and evaluates resources available to the programs and utilizes in a fiscally responsible manner Qualifications Required Qualifications: Doctorate in Nursing and Master’s Degree in Nursing Eligibility for NJ licensure or Compact license 10 or more years of full-time nursing faculty experience in a baccalaureate or higher degree program. Administrative experience in an academic setting with demonstrated leadership in curriculum development and evaluation Scholarly activity in nursing education, practice or leadership Preferred Qualifications: Experience with nursing accreditation and State Board accreditation Professional certification Experience with innovative technology across the nursing curricula New program development Application Materials Cover Letter indicating interest and qualifications Curriculum Vitae Copies of certifications and licenses Statement of leadership philosophy and potential directions for nursing education at Ramapo College (3 pages maximum) Review of applications will begin on May 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Supplemental Information EEO Statement: Ramapo College is an Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Ramapo has a long history of advocating, advising, and supporting diversity, equity, and inclusiveness. Examples can be found in its mission statement, strategic plans, degree and course offerings, community outreach programs, and other diversity programs. Ramapo’s commitment to diversity and inclusion is infused across all facets of the College; where the environment is welcoming, dedicated to social justice, respectful of freedom of expression, focused on educating and having an ongoing conversation regarding cultural competence and the benefits and importance of diversity. Ramapo offers a comprehensive benefits package through the State of New Jersey to full-time employees including health care, dental, prescription drug plans, retirement, pension, deferred compensation plans, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, holidays, vacation, and sick leave. To learn more details, visit our benefits page. 01 Do you have a Doctorate in Nursing and a Master’s Degree in Nursing? yes no 02 Do you have 10 or more years of full-time nursing faculty experience in a baccalaureate or higher degree program?  And administrative experience in an academic setting with demonstrated leadership in curriculum development and evaluation? yes no Required Question Employer Ramapo College of New Jersey Address 505 Ramapo Valley Road Mahwah, New Jersey, 07430 Phone 2016847782 Website https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ramapo? Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026